{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/nernst-equation/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/nernst-equation.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Nernst Equation | Chemistry","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Electrochemistry &amp; Redox\n      </a>\n      <!-- Progress indicator -->\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-indigo-400 to-violet-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -square-root-variable text-indigo-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Nernst Equation\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding how concentration affects electrode potential and predicting cell voltages under non-standard conditions.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-indigo-50 border-l-4 border-indigo-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-indigo-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• State the Nernst equation and identify each term</li>\n          <li>• Calculate electrode potential at non-standard concentrations</li>\n          <li>• Predict cell potential under varying conditions</li>\n          <li>• Understand the relationship between E, E°, and concentration</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: Introduction -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          What is the Nernst Equation?\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">\n            The <strong class=\"text-indigo-600\">Nernst equation</strong> relates the electrode potential of a half-cell or overall cell to the standard electrode potential, temperature, and activities (approximately concentrations) of the chemical species undergoing reduction and oxidation.\n          </p>\n          \n          <div class=\"formula-box p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-bold text-indigo-800 mb-3 text-center\">The Nernst Equation</h3>\n            <div class=\"bg-white/50 p-4 rounded-lg text-center\">\n              <p class=\"text-2xl font-mono text-indigo-800 font-bold\">E = E° - (RT/nF) ln Q</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3\">Where:</h4>\n            <div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-sm\">\n              <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-2 rounded\">\n                <p class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-700\">E</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Cell potential (V)</p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-2 rounded\">\n                <p class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-700\">E°</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Standard cell potential (V)</p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-2 rounded\">\n                <p class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-700\">R</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Gas constant (8.314 J/mol·K)</p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-2 rounded\">\n                <p class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-700\">T</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Temperature (K)</p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-2 rounded\">\n                <p class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-700\">n</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Number of electrons transferred</p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-2 rounded\">\n                <p class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-700\">F</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Faraday constant (96,500 C/mol)</p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-2 rounded col-span-2 md:col-span-1\">\n                <p class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-700\">Q</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Reaction quotient</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Simplified Form -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Simplified Form at 25°C\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">At room temperature (25°C = 298 K), the Nernst equation can be simplified by substituting the constants and converting from natural log to base-10 log:</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"formula-box p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white/50 p-4 rounded-lg text-center\">\n              <p class=\"text-2xl font-mono text-indigo-800 font-bold\">E = E° - (0.059/n) log Q</p>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"text-center text-sm text-indigo-700 mt-2\">At 25°C (298 K)</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Key Point</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">The factor 0.059 comes from: (RT/F) × ln(10) = (8.314 × 298 / 96500) × 2.303 ≈ 0.059 V</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: The Reaction Quotient -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Calculating the Reaction Quotient (Q)\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">For a general reaction: <strong>aA + bB → cC + dD</strong></p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n            <p class=\"text-center font-mono text-lg text-indigo-700\">Q = [C]<sup>c</sup> [D]<sup>d</sup> / [A]<sup>a</sup> [B]<sup>b</sup></p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-4\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -info-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"info\">info</span>Important Rules</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• <strong>Solids and pure liquids</strong> have activity = 1 (not included in Q)</li>\n              <li>• <strong>Gases</strong> use partial pressures (in atm)</li>\n              <li>• <strong>Aqueous ions</strong> use molar concentrations</li>\n              <li>• Water as a solvent has activity ≈ 1</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2\">At Equilibrium</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Q = K (equilibrium constant)</p>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">E = 0 (no driving force)</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-rose-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-rose-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-rose-700 mb-2\">Standard Conditions</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">All concentrations = 1 M</p>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Q = 1, log Q = 0, so E = E°</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Worked Examples -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Worked Examples\n        </h2>\n        \n        <!-- Example 1 -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-indigo-50 text-left font-semibold text-indigo-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-indigo-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-indigo-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Example 1: Calculate Cell Potential</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">\n                Calculate the potential of a Daniel cell: Zn|Zn²⁺(0.01 M)||Cu²⁺(0.1 M)|Cu\n              </p>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 mb-3\">Given: E°(Zn²⁺/Zn) = -0.76 V, E°(Cu²⁺/Cu) = +0.34 V</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-indigo-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Calculate E°cell</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-indigo-700 font-mono mt-1\">E°cell = E°cathode - E°anode = +0.34 - (-0.76) = +1.10 V</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Write the cell reaction and Q</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 font-mono mt-1\">Zn + Cu²⁺ → Zn²⁺ + Cu</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 font-mono mt-1\">Q = [Zn²⁺] / [Cu²⁺] = 0.01 / 0.1 = 0.1</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Apply Nernst equation (n = 2)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E = E° - (0.059/n) log Q</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E = 1.10 - (0.059/2) log(0.1)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E = 1.10 - (0.0295) × (-1)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E = 1.10 + 0.0295 = <strong>1.13 V</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: E = 1.13 V (higher than E° because [Cu²⁺] &gt; [Zn²⁺])</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Example 2 -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-purple-50 text-left font-semibold text-purple-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-purple-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -flask mr-2 text-purple-500\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>Example 2: Electrode Potential</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">\n                Calculate the potential of a hydrogen electrode when [H⁺] = 0.01 M and H₂ is at 1 atm.\n              </p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Write the half-reaction</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700 font-mono mt-1\">2H⁺ + 2e⁻ → H₂ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; E° = 0.00 V</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Calculate Q</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 font-mono mt-1\">Q = PH₂ / [H⁺]² = 1 / (0.01)² = 1 / 0.0001 = 10000</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Apply Nernst equation (n = 2)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E = E° - (0.059/n) log Q</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E = 0.00 - (0.059/2) log(10000)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E = 0.00 - 0.0295 × 4</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E = <strong>-0.118 V</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: E = -0.118 V (lower pH means lower potential)</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Effect of Concentration -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Effect of Concentration on Cell Potential\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -arrow-up mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_upward\">arrow_upward</span>Increasing Products</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Q increases → log Q is positive → E &lt; E°</p>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-xs mt-2\">Cell potential decreases</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -arrow-down mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_downward\">arrow_downward</span>Increasing Reactants</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Q decreases → log Q is negative → E &gt; E°</p>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-xs mt-2\">Cell potential increases</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -balance-scale mr-2\" data-mi=\"balance\">balance</span>Le Chatelier's Principle</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">The Nernst equation shows that cells \"prefer\" to run when reactants are concentrated and products are dilute. This aligns with Le Chatelier's principle: high reactant concentration drives the reaction forward, giving a higher cell potential.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Video -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">6</span>\n          Video: The Nernst Equation\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n          <div class=\"video-container\">\n            <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/oOjGi6fGbVk\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 7: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-7\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-indigo-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Calculate E for the cell: Zn|Zn²⁺(0.1 M)||Cu²⁺(0.001 M)|Cu</p>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2\">E°cell = 1.10 V</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Q = [Zn²⁺]/[Cu²⁺] = 0.1/0.001 = 100</p>\n                <p>E = 1.10 - (0.059/2) log(100)</p>\n                <p>E = 1.10 - 0.0295 × 2</p>\n                <p><strong>Answer: E = 1.04 V</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. What is the potential of a Cu²⁺/Cu electrode when [Cu²⁺] = 0.001 M? (E° = +0.34 V)</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu</p>\n                <p>Q = 1/[Cu²⁺] = 1/0.001 = 1000</p>\n                <p>E = 0.34 - (0.059/2) log(1000)</p>\n                <p>E = 0.34 - 0.0295 × 3</p>\n                <p><strong>Answer: E = 0.25 V</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. At what concentration of Cu²⁺ will the Cu²⁺/Cu electrode have a potential of 0.28 V? (E° = +0.34 V)</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>E = E° - (0.059/2) log(1/[Cu²⁺])</p>\n                <p>0.28 = 0.34 - 0.0295 log(1/[Cu²⁺])</p>\n                <p>0.0295 log(1/[Cu²⁺]) = 0.06</p>\n                <p>log(1/[Cu²⁺]) = 2.03</p>\n                <p>1/[Cu²⁺] = 10²·⁰³ ≈ 107</p>\n                <p><strong>Answer: [Cu²⁺] ≈ 0.0093 M (or about 0.01 M)</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-8\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-indigo-50 to-violet-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-indigo-200\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n          <ul class=\"text-indigo-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n            <li>• <strong>Nernst Equation:</strong> E = E° - (RT/nF) ln Q or E = E° - (0.059/n) log Q (at 25°C)</li>\n            <li>• Q uses product concentrations in the numerator, reactants in the denominator</li>\n            <li>• Solids and pure liquids have activity = 1</li>\n            <li>• Higher reactant concentration → lower Q → higher E (more driving force)</li>\n            <li>• At equilibrium: E = 0 and Q = K</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Scripts -->\n  \n\n  <!-- Topic Tracking and Quiz System -->\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-indigo-50 to-violet-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n    }\n    .accordion-content {\n      max-height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;\n    }\n    .accordion-content.open {\n      max-height: 2000px;\n    }\n    .step-card {\n      transition: all 0.2s ease;\n    }\n    .step-card:hover {\n      transform: translateX(4px);\n    }\n    .formula-box {\n      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e0e7ff 0%, #c7d2fe 100%);\n      border: 2px solid #6366f1;\n    }\n    #topic-complete-btn {\n      transition: all 0.3s ease;\n    }\n    #topic-complete-btn:not(:disabled):hover {\n      transform: scale(1.02);\n    }\n    .video-container {\n      position: relative;\n      width: 100%;\n      padding-bottom: 56.25%;\n      height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      border-radius: 8px;\n      background: #f9fafb;\n    }\n    .video-container iframe {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 0; left: 0;\n      width: 100%;\n      height: 100%;\n      border: none;\n    }"],"quiz":{"topicId":"nernst-equation","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"What does the Nernst equation calculate?","options":["Standard electrode potential","Cell potential at non-standard conditions","Equilibrium constant","Rate of reaction"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The Nernst equation calculates the electrode or cell potential under non-standard conditions of concentration, pressure, or temperature."},{"question":"What is the simplified form of the Nernst equation at 25°C?","options":["E = E° - (RT/nF) ln Q","E = E° - (0.059/n) log Q","E = E° + (RT/nF) ln Q","E = E° × Q"],"correct":1,"explanation":"At 25°C, the constants combine to give: E = E° - (0.059/n) log Q, where 0.059 is a convenient constant."},{"question":"In the Nernst equation, what does Q represent?","options":["Charge transferred","Reaction quotient","Heat of reaction","Electrode constant"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Q is the reaction quotient - the ratio of product concentrations to reactant concentrations at any point in the reaction."},{"question":"What happens to cell potential when reactant concentration increases?","options":["E decreases","E increases","E stays the same","E becomes negative"],"correct":1,"explanation":"When reactants increase, Q decreases, log Q becomes more negative, so E = E° - (positive)×(negative) = E° + positive, meaning E increases."},{"question":"Calculate E for a cell with E° = 1.10 V, n = 2, and Q = 100.","options":["1.04 V","1.16 V","1.10 V","0.98 V"],"correct":0,"explanation":"E = E° - (0.059/n) log Q = 1.10 - (0.059/2) × log(100) = 1.10 - 0.0295 × 2 = 1.10 - 0.059 = 1.04 V"},{"question":"At equilibrium, what is the value of E?","options":["E = E°","E = 0","E = -E°","E = infinity"],"correct":1,"explanation":"At equilibrium, there is no net driving force for the reaction, so E = 0. Also, at equilibrium Q = K (the equilibrium constant)."},{"question":"What is the activity of a pure solid in the Nernst equation?","options":["0","1","Its molar mass","Its concentration"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Pure solids and pure liquids have activity = 1 by definition, so they don't appear in the Q expression."},{"question":"If [Cu²⁺] = 0.01 M in a Cu²⁺/Cu half-cell (E° = +0.34 V), what is E?","options":["0.34 V","0.28 V","0.40 V","0.22 V"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Q = 1/[Cu²⁺] = 100. E = 0.34 - (0.059/2) log(100) = 0.34 - 0.0295 × 2 = 0.34 - 0.059 = 0.28 V"}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"nernst-equation","topicTitle":"Nernst Equation","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6","section-7","section-8"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}